---
source: crates/biome_js_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.vue
---
# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <div v-memo="{x}" />
  <div v-memo="a ? {b} : c+d" />
  <div v-memo="(a,{b},c(),d+1)" />
  <div v-memo="()=>42" />
  <div v-memo="function () { return [] }" />
  <div v-memo="a=42" />
  <div v-memo="'string'" />
  <div v-memo="42" />
  <div v-memo="null" />
  <div v-memo="`template ${x}`" />
  <div v-memo="!x" />
  <div v-memo="typeof x" />
  <div v-memo="x++" />
  <div v-memo="--x" />
  <div v-memo="'a' in x" />
  <div v-memo="x instanceof Array" />
  <div v-memo="class {}" />
  <div v-memo="({ x })" />
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.vue:3:16 lint/nursery/useVueValidVMemo ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The value of v-memo must be an array, but this expression never produces one.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <div v-memo="{x}" />
      │                ^^^
    4 │   <div v-memo="a ? {b} : c+d" />
    5 │   <div v-memo="(a,{b},c(),d+1)" />
  
  i Vue skips updating this element until one of the values in the v-memo array changes, so it needs an array to compare.
  
  i Put the values in square brackets, for example v-memo="[item.id, selected]".
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

